@startuml deploy-path-ceilings
' ============================================================================
' The deploy path end-to-end, with each Theta(depth) traversal's MEASURED
' maximum source-nesting depth on the 2 MiB stack a tokio worker gets.
'   RED   #C62828 aborts the node (SIGSEGV on the guard page -> abort)
'   AMBER #EF6C00 still bounded
'   GREEN #2E7D32 no ceiling below the search bound
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam roundcorner 8

title <b>The deploy path, and where each ceiling sits</b>\nmaximum source nesting depth on a **2 MiB** tokio worker

|#ECEFF1|network|
start
:gRPC `DeployService/doDeploy`\n`deploy_grpc_service_v1.rs:256`\ninbound cap **16 MiB**;

|#FFF3E0|ingress (pre-consensus, pre-storage, NO budget in scope)|
:`block_api.rs:477  deploy_cosigned`\n**synchronous, inline on the tokio worker**\n(no `spawn_blocking`);
:`dispatch.rs:66` → `block_admission.rs:105`\n`admit_deploy` / `admit_deploy_cosigned`;
note right #FFEBEE
  **BEFORE** — `Ok(_parsed_term)`, bound with a
  leading underscore, never read, released at the
  closing brace by the derived recursive
  `drop_in_place::<Par>` at **96.0 B/level**.
  ⇒ ceiling **21,781**; depth **21,782** = exit 134.
  43,565 bytes of source abort the node.
end note
:**AFTER** — `validate_deploy_term`\nparses, then hands the term to\n`par_children::dismantle`\n(an explicit `Vec<Par>` worklist);
note right #E8F5E9
  **0.0 B/level**, no ceiling below **262,144**.
  Control (the pre-repair shape, same binary,
  same signed deploy) still caps at 21,782.
end note

|#E3F2FD|storage + consensus|
:admission stores `Signed<DeployData>`\n— the **source string**, never a `Par`;
:proposer **re-normalizes** from source\n`acceptance.rs:321`;

|#FFF3E0|evaluation|
:`InterpreterImpl::inj_attempt`\n build-normalized-term  →  set-initial-cost  →  reduce;
note right #FFF3E0
  **`normalize`** (source → `Par`): CONVERTED,
  0 B/level, survives depth <latex>\geq</latex> 39,960.
  **`inj_attempt` set-initial-cost**: was a
  write-then-read-back `source_process().cloned()`
  at **2,852 B/level** ⇒ ceiling **729**;
  now `into_source_process()` (by move),
  0 B/level, <latex>\geq 1{,}048{,}576</latex>.
end note
:reduction — `substitute_and_charge` on the send path;
note right #E8F5E9
  **`plain_deploy`**  286  →  **6,831**  (**23.9<latex>\times</latex>**)
  MEASURED again 2026-07-29: **6,831**, 6,832 exits 134.
end note
:reduction — a deep value arriving over a COMM binder;
note right #FFEBEE
  **`env_get_deploy`** — the CONTROL.
  Recorded 283 before and after the send-path repair.
  ⚠ MEASURED at HEAD 2026-07-29: **274**
  (275 exits 134) — see §7.4, the control has
  drifted 9 levels since it was recorded.
  `Env::get` returns its value **cloned**, and the
  copy **is** the meaning of substitution.
end note
stop

legend bottom
  |= ceiling |= subject |= status |
